Give read_config() a real prototype.

cfgfile.h declared read_config() with an empty parameter list, which C23
reads as "takes no arguments", so the call in iftop.c is no longer valid:

  iftop.c:803:16: warning: passing arguments to 'read_config' without a
  prototype is deprecated in all versions of C and is not supported in
  C23 [-Wdeprecated-non-prototype]

Declare it as defined in cfgfile.c, and spell the neighbouring
config_init() as (void) while here.

--- a/cfgfile.h
+++ b/cfgfile.h
@@ -13,13 +13,13 @@
     int value;
 } config_enumeration_type;
 
-int read_config();
+int read_config(char *file, int whinge_on_error);
 
 char *config_get_string(const char *directive);
 int config_get_bool(const char *directive);
 int config_get_int(const char *directive, int *value);
 int config_get_float(const char *directive, float *value);
-int config_init();
+int config_init(void);
 void config_set_string(const char *directive, const char* s);
 int config_get_enum(const char *directive, config_enumeration_type *enumeration, int *value);
 
